'''''Peperomia galioides''''' is a species of [[plant]] in the family [[Piperaceae]], native to [[Mexico]], [[Central America]] and [[South America]].<ref>{{Cite web|title=Peperomia galioides Kunth {{!}} Plants of the World Online {{!}} Kew Science|url=http://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:678659-1|access-date=2021-05-04|website=Plants of the World Online|language=en}}</ref> ''P. galioides'' has [[Petiole (botany)|petioles]] of less than 1mm long and leaves between 5-30mm.<ref>{{cite book | title=Flora of the Galápagos Islands | url=https://archive.org/details/floraofgalapagos0000wigg | url-access=registration | publisher=Stanford University Press, 1971 |author1=L. Wiggins, Ira |author2=M. Porter, Duncan | isbn=978-0804707329| year=1971 }}</ref> There has been research in Colombia and Peru to know about the essential oils of this species.<ref>{{cite journal | title=Journal of Essential Oil Research |author1=Robayo-Gama, Paola A |author2=E. Quijano, Clara |author3=Morales, Gustavo |author4=A Pino. Jorge | journal=Composition of the Essential Oil from Leaves of Peperomia Galioides HBK Grown in Colombia |date=August 2008 | volume=22 | issue=4 | pages=307–309 | doi=10.1080/10412905.2010.9700332|s2cid=95937599 }}</ref><ref name=":0" /> It was traditionally used in Peruvian herbal medicine.<ref name=":0">{{cite journal | url=http://www.relaquim.com/archive/2007/p2007351-2-7.pdf |author1=Di Leo Lira, Paola |author2=Farfán, Yoni |author3=M. van Baren, Catalina |author4=L. Bandoni, Arnaldo |author5=D. Coussio, Jorge |author6=Pastor De Abram, Ana | title=Composition of the Essential Oil of Two Peperomia from Peru}}</ref>

